SendmailAnalyzer 10 for Debian
==============================

SendmailAnalyzer 10.0.16 is packaged for Debian 13. Installing with APT resolves
the Perl/SQLite/Plack/ACL dependencies, creates the service account, prepares
least-privilege read access to current and rotated logs, validates SQLite and
then enables/restarts the v10 collector and web services on a running systemd
host.

An existing v10 SQLite database is authoritative and is preserved across normal
package upgrades. Fresh installations initialize an empty v10 SQLite database.
SendmailAnalyzer 9.4 data is NOT imported or retired automatically by current
package revisions. Legacy migration helpers remain available only for explicit,
manual use; see MIGRATION-9.4.md.

Before a v10 upgrade, the package creates rollback material under
/var/backups/sendmailanalyzer/ and validates the current SQLite database. If the
post-install validation fails, it attempts to restore the previous database and
SendmailAnalyzer service state.

Configuration:
  /etc/sendmailanalyzer.conf
  /usr/share/doc/sendmailanalyzer/CONFIGURATION.md

Dependencies:
  /usr/share/doc/sendmailanalyzer/DEPENDENCIES.md

Legacy migration policy:
  /usr/share/doc/sendmailanalyzer/MIGRATION-9.4.md

The PSGI web service listens on 127.0.0.1:9080 by default and is intended to be
published through a reverse proxy such as Apache.

Site-local overrides and private header mappings belong in:

  /etc/sendmailanalyzer.d/*.conf

The package does not own or replace files in that directory.
